# ============================================================
# Line-ending normalisation — versioned deliberately.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE.
#
# The drift gate (`node design-system/build/build.mjs --check`) works by
# BYTE-COMPARING a freshly generated artifact against the committed copy. That
# comparison is the mechanism that makes token drift impossible — and it is
# exactly as strong as the guarantee that a checkout reproduces the committed
# bytes.
#
# It did not. `core.autocrlf=false` and `core.eol=lf` were set in .git/config,
# which is machine-local and does NOT travel with a clone. On Windows a fresh
# clone instead inherits `autocrlf=true` from the system gitconfig, checks out
# every generated artifact with CRLF, and the drift gate reports all six as
# drifted against a source that has not changed. Verified by cloning: the blob
# holds 3,949 bytes with 0 CRLF, the clone's working file 4,074 with 125.
#
# The failure is worse than a false alarm. A gate that fails on a clean clone is
# a gate people learn to ignore, and the instruction it prints — "Run:
# build.mjs" — silently rewrites all six artifacts to CRLF and commits a
# whole-file diff that hides any real change inside it.
#
# So normalisation is declared in the repository, where it is part of the
# contract, rather than in one machine's config where it is a coincidence.
# ============================================================

# Everything is text and checks out LF, on every platform. Git still detects
# binary content by inspection and leaves it alone, so this is safe for any
# file type; the explicit rules below are belt-and-braces for the ones where
# corruption would be silent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Visual-parity baselines. A byte-for-byte contract — never touched, never
# diffed as text. (Also LFS-tracked by "Onboarding Flow/.gitattributes", whose
# deeper rules win for the paths it covers; repeated here so the guarantee does
# not depend on that file's continued existence.)
*.png  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary

# Lockfiles: LF, and not worth diffing by hand.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff
